    "test:matrix:all": "npm run test:prediction:bank-health && npm run test:practice:weightage-mix && npm run test:canonical:generator && npm run test:trig:retire && npm run test:llm:path-audit && npm run test:bsre:path && npm run test:topickey:guard && npm run test:topickey:runtime && npm run test:qr:channel && npm run test:objective:dedup && npm run test:tutor:visual-catalogue && npm run test:ci:convergence && npm run test:tutor:ci-overlay && npm run test:tutor:qp-overlay && npm run test:server:rate-limit && npm run test:server:token-instrumentation && npm run test:server:admin-telemetry && npm run test:server:verified-caller && npm run test:server:check-solution && npm run test:server:entitlement && npm run test:server:http-utils && npm run test:server:session-store && npm run test:server:warm-pool-gate && npm run test:server:account-erasure && npm run test:server:account-erasure-route && npm run test:server:account-export && npm run test:server:account-export-route && npm run test:server:spawned-loader-resolution && npm run test:server:tutor-cache && npm run test:server:eval-parity && npm run test:ci:docs-lane && npm run test:scope-guard:blindspot && npm run test:repo-boundary && npm run test:mojibake",
    "_comment:test:matrix:all": "★ [GUARD-3] THE THREE GUARD SELF-TESTS RUN AT THE TAIL, DELIBERATELY. GUARD-2 (#565/#568) wired scope-guard:blindspot and repo-boundary as the FIRST two links; GUARD-3 moves them to the tail and adds test:mojibake, whose npm script existed on trunk but which no chain invoked at all. ★ WHY THE TAIL: this is an && chain, so whatever runs first MASKS everything after it on failure. These three are ACCEPTANCE SUITES FOR THE GUARDS THEMSELVES, not checks on the PR's scope — putting the newest, least battle-tested suites in front lets a wobble in guard tooling hide ~19 established content and server gates. The fail-fast argument does not apply: the real scope check is `scope:guard`, which runs pre-commit and separately. The ordering is not left to this comment — `test:repo-boundary` asserts `guard_self_tests_run_at_matrix_tail` against this very string, so front-loading a self-test again turns the matrix red. DO NOT FRONT-LOAD A SELF-TEST. ★ [CI-DOCS] test:server:http-utils and test:server:session-store were added by SEC-1 (#596), were green locally, and were gated by NOTHING — no chain invoked them, exactly the shape Wave 2 found over artifacts/api-server. They are wired here now, and the wiring is no longer a one-off promise: test:ci:docs-lane ENUMERATES every server/**/*.test.cjs FROM DISK and fails when one of them is missing from this string, so the NEXT unwired suite goes red instead of silent. [FU-SEC1-CI-WIRE-SERVER-TESTS]",
